    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "S T. P A T R I C K S, L A H I N C H, C O. C L A R E V95 H6T4\r\n\r\nA UNIQUE COASTAL HOME OFFERING BEACH, BAY,  OCEAN AND GOLF COURSE VIEWS IN A PRIVATE ‘CUL DE SAC’ LOCATION\r\nAN EXCEPTIONAL LOCATION – SMELL THE SEA AIR AND LISTEN TO THE RELAXING BEACH SOUNDS ALL YEAR ROUND.\r\n\r\nCOMPANY LICENCE NO 003178\r\n\r\nL O C A T I O N\r\n\r\nDETACHED 4 BEDROOM BEACH PROPERTY IN A HIGHLY SOUGHT AFTER LOCATION!\r\n\r\nThis is an impressive bungalow home located in a private ‘cul de sac’ accessed from the N67 - Lahinch, Miltown Malbay and Spanish Point main route. This property enables one to step onto Lahinch Promenade within a 2 minute stroll. \r\n\r\nLahinch is one of the best known and most visited seaside resorts in Ireland that generations of people have enjoyed down through the years. Its beautiful sandy beach stretches for 2km and in recent years has become a ‘surfers paradise’ attracting people and visitors worldwide all year round to its many surf schools. It is considered to be the ideal family location to discover, explore and enjoy the North Clare and West Clare rugged coastline. \r\n\r\nLahinch Golf Club, celebrating the prestigious Walker Cup in September this year following on from The Dubai Duty Free Irish Open in 2019 is always an extremely popular venue attraction to golfers across the globe to play on the 18 hole renowned championship course.\r\n\r\nLahinch primary school and local creche are both just a short walk from the property.\r\n\r\nEnjoy Lahinch Leisure Centre on Lahinch Promenade, overlooking the Atlantic Ocean. Lahinch Leisure Centre has a superb gym and 25m heated pool, learner's pool, steam room and jacuzzi. Swimming lessons are available for all age groups.\r\n\r\nThe famous Cliffs of Moher are within a 10-minute drive of Lahinch. Continue to Doolin, the home of traditional Irish music and onto Doolin Pier offering daily boat trips to the Aran Islands.\r\n\r\nEnnistymon, a 3km drive from Lahinch, is the nearest shopping town, a warm and friendly town with a selection of excellent schools, shops, local crèche facilities, medical facilities, banks, post office and a host of other commercial facilities all on the doorstep.\r\n\r\nNew, modern ‘state of the art’ building (Ennistymon Community School) is the main secondary school located on the Lahinch Road, Ennistymon.\r\n\r\nD E S C R I P T I O N\r\nProperties of this calibre are infrequent to the market and in its entirety this property offers a unique opportunity to acquire a character filled \r\nfamily home in a highly sought after location. Situated in a quiet and private ‘cul de sac’, this property is instantly captivating and uplifting on \r\ninspection. The property presents a quirky style created by the owner and a viewing, highly recommended, is guaranteed not to disappoint.\r\n\r\nThis is a prime location, presenting a charming property boasting spacious, bright and well laid out accommodation situated within a 2 minute stroll from the beginning of Lahinch Promenade and beach, central to all required amenities and services, hotels, bars and award winning restaurants. This property offers an amazing opportunity to acquire a first floor, subject to planning permission making the most of Lahinch beach, Liscannor Bay and Atlantic Ocean views if desired. The property is in turnkey order and its location could not be better.\r\n\r\nAccommodation is comprised of an entrance L shaped hallway, an open plan galley styled kitchen/living/dining room, 4 spacious bedrooms and a main bathroom. Gas operated central heating. A solid fuel cook stove creates a cosy living/dining area creating that perfect ambience. Double glazed wood grain pvc windows and doors.\r\n\r\nAmple off street private parking to the front of the property. A brick paved rear patio runs the length of the house. A spacious shed adjacent is fully insulated and boasts ideal storage space which can be accessed by doors at both front and rear. \r\nThe front parking area of the property has been finished in a Wexford grit sand. The property has a definite boundary wall to front, sides and rear with 2 pillars at the driveway entrance.\r\n\r\nBER C.\r\nFLOOR AREA 74.51 SQ. M.\r\nYEAR CONSTRUCTED 1972\r\n\r\nA C C O M M O D A T I O N\r\n(A P P R O X I M A T E   D I M E N S I O N S)\r\n\r\nEntrance Hall: (3.45m x 1.48m) plus (7.36m x 0.88m) L shaped hallway, tiled flooring at entrance and corridor has a wood effect tile finish, corridor leading to bedrooms and main bathroom.\r\n\r\nLiving/dining: (5.36m x 3.58m) Dual aspect with views of Lahinch beach, Liscannor bay and O’ Briens castle at the Cliffs of Moher across the Atlantic Ocean. Solid fuel cook top stove with a quirky brick feature above the timber mantle, tiled wainscotting, timber flooring, open plan to the kitchen. This is an extremely spacious and bright room. 2 pendant light points.\r\n\r\nGalley kitchen: (3.82m x 1.86m) A well organised and efficient Galley styled kitchen complete with tiled flooring and full wall tiling, ample work top space, sink and fitted base units in a white finish, handmade wall mounted timber display units and door to the rear with a cap flap. Ceiling spotlighting. \r\nThe kitchen has a dishwasher, washing machine and fridge freezer. A new 5 ring gas operated hob with extractor, grill and cooker has just been installed. New gas boiler installed.\r\n\r\nMain bathroom: (2.66m x 1.84m) Fully tiled, tiled windowsill, complete with bath, spacious mains rain shower unit with a shower panel folding door, W.C., W.H.B., towel radiator, tiled wall inserts, tongue and groove timber ceiling and wall mounted heater. Rear aspect.\r\n\r\nBedroom 1: (3m x 2.40m) Front aspect with views of the Lahinch beach and Liscannor Bay, tiled wood affect timber flooring. Front aspect, bright and spacious.\r\n\r\nBedroom 2: (3m x 2.40m) Front aspect with views of the Liscannor Bay and Lahinch Beach, tiled wood affect timber flooring. Front aspect, again another bright bedroom boasting stunning beach and bay views. Pendant light point.\r\n\r\nBedroom 3: (3.47m x 3.14m) Front aspect with views of the Liscannor Bay and Lahinch beach, tiled wood affect timber flooring, over bed wall mounted reading lighting plus pendant light point.\r\n\r\nBedroom 4: (2.69m x 2.38m) + (1.84m x 1.31m) L shaped, rear aspect, tiled wood affect timber flooring, over bed wall mounted reading lighting plus pendant light point. Spacious and bright bedroom. \r\n\r\nTHIS PROPERTY IS IDEALLY SUITABLE AS AN IMPRESSIVE FAMILY RESIDENCE OR A HOLIDAY GETAWAY."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Features",
        "SortOrder": 3,
        "Content": "Stunning clear views of Lahinch beach, Liscannor Bay, O’ Brien’s tower at the Cliffs of Moher over the Atlantic from the property.\r\nA four-bedroom property presented in a quirky beach style, turnkey order, ready for immediate occupancy.\r\nWithin a 2 minute stroll to Lahinch promenade, beach, hotels, bars, award winning restaurants and all amenities and facilities in the town.\r\nThis property has ample onsite parking at the front of the property.\r\nNew tiled and timber flooring throughout. Freshly painted. All architrave and skirting completed in white.\r\nNew gas boiler installed.\r\n4 ring gas operated hob, cooker and grill just installed.\r\nAccessed by a private ‘cul de sac’ driveway.\r\nLiscannor flag paved patio to the front of the property.\r\nOffers an opportunity to add a first floor subject to planning permission if desired."
      },
